{"parentUuid":"cd004032-38db-4000-a2c5-68a600afb5bf","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CeLvHEqHUs1s4LaZkGv1S","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Confirmed the gaps. Let me file one comprehensive tracking issue."}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2068,"cache_read_input_tokens":521917,"output_tokens":2745,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":706},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2068,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2745,"cache_read_input_tokens":521917,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2068,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2068},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeLvHBoy4GQ9cSSf3AkG7","type":"assistant","uuid":"f28034a9-b3fe-4e40-8f2d-bd8c2e251889","timestamp":"2026-08-24T04:11:08.075Z","effort":"high","session_id":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream","sessionId":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","version":"2.1.228","gitBranch":"feat/bigquery-auto-create-table","slug":"linear-noodling-leaf"}
{"parentUuid":"f28034a9-b3fe-4e40-8f2d-bd8c2e251889","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CeLvHEqHUs1s4LaZkGv1S","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01BFAGYbLwD19vdN5cQVfGDE","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream\ngh auth switch --user PawanSikawat >/dev/null 2>&1\nXSINK_URL=$(gh issue create --repo faucet-hq/faucet-stream \\\n  --title \"feat(sinks): consistent auto-create-table (schema-inferred) across all table-based sinks\" \\\n  --label enhancement --label tier-2 \\\n  --body \"$(cat <<'BODY'\n## Summary\nGeneralize the BigQuery `create_table` behavior (#578) into a **consistent auto-create-table capability across every table-based sink**: when the destination table (and, where applicable, its schema/dataset/database) does not exist, create it from the schema inferred over the first written page — controlled by a uniform `create_table: bool` config field, defaulting to `true` (a first-ever sync can't assume the target exists). Set `false` to require a pre-existing target and fail fast.\n\n## Motivation\nMigrating the 47 Meltano taps surfaced this on BigQuery (#578): a first sync to a fresh destination failed because the sink required the table to pre-exist. Every table-based destination has the same first-sync problem. Today the behavior is **inconsistent** across sinks — some auto-map columns, some have a `create_table` flag with different defaults/scope, and several can't create a table at all. A single, predictable `create_table` contract (same field name, same default, same schema-inference rules) makes every SQL/warehouse sink usable on a first run and removes per-connector surprises. Ties to the Primary Goal (reliability) and connector ergonomics.\n\n## Current state (audit)\n**Full auto-create (done):**\n- `bigquery` — `create_table` (default `true`), infers schema from first page, handles missing **and** schemaless tables, all write modes (#578).\n\n**Has *some* create/auto-map logic — needs review for consistency (field name, default, schema inference, write-mode coverage):**\n- `postgres`, `mysql`, `sqlite` — `auto_map` column mode (verify it actually CREATEs a missing table vs requires it to exist).\n- `mssql` — `create_table` exists but is **`json_column`-mode only** and defaults **`false`** (inconsistent with the proposed default `true` + full column inference).\n- `snowflake`, `spanner`, `duckdb`, `delta`, `iceberg` — verify current create/evolve behavior and align to the contract (iceberg/delta are table-format sinks; dataset/namespace creation differs).\n\n**No create-table capability (the gaps):**\n- `clickhouse` — no `CREATE TABLE`; requires the table to pre-exist.\n- `redshift` — no `CREATE TABLE`; requires the table to pre-exist.\n\n**Implicit auto-create (schemaless targets — decide whether to add an explicit knob for parity):**\n- `mongodb` (collections auto-create on first insert), `elasticsearch` (indices auto-create / dynamic mapping).\n\n**Not applicable (no table concept):**\n- `jsonl`, `csv`, `stdout`, `s3`, `gcs`, `parquet`, `azure-blob`, `sftp`, `http`, `kafka`, `redis`, `nats`, `pubsub`, `sqs`, `kinesis`.\n\n## Proposed design\n- A shared config surface: `create_table: bool` (default `true`) on every table-based sink, plus per-dialect location/namespace/database creation where relevant (`location` for BigQuery; schema for postgres; database/engine for clickhouse; etc.).\n- Shared schema-inference helper in `faucet-core` (map an `infer_schema`-shaped object to a dialect's column types) so each sink's `CREATE TABLE` generator is thin and consistent (mirrors the existing `json_schema_base_type` / `SqlBaseType` used by schema-drift evolve).\n- Readiness check = \"target exists with a usable schema\"; create/replace only when missing or schemaless; never drop a schema'd table.\n- Honor `create_table: false` with a clear, uniform error.\n- Compose with the existing schema-drift `evolve` policy (#194) for later-column additions.\n\n## Affected crates\n`crates/sink/{clickhouse,redshift,mssql,postgres,mysql,sqlite,snowflake,spanner,duckdb,delta,iceberg,mongodb,elasticsearch}`, a shared helper in `faucet-core`, the `create_table` docs in each README + `docs/book/src/reference/connectors.md`, and `schemas/faucet.schema.json`.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- Every table-based sink exposes `create_table` (default `true`) and auto-creates a missing target from the first page's inferred schema; `clickhouse` and `redshift` gain the capability.\n- `mssql` default/scope aligned to the shared contract; `postgres`/`mysql`/`sqlite`/`snowflake`/`spanner`/`duckdb`/`delta`/`iceberg` verified/aligned.\n- Consistent field name + default + error across sinks; unit + integration tests per sink; capability documented in each README and the connector reference.\n\n## Out of scope\n- Reconciling a data page against a wrong pre-existing schema (that is schema-drift `evolve`, #194).\n- Non-table sinks.\n\n## References\nPattern: #578 (BigQuery). Roadmap epic: #38.\nBODY\n)\" 2>&1 | grep -vE \"setValueForKey|valueForKey\" | grep -E \"https://github.com/faucet-hq\" | head -1)\necho \"XSINK_ISSUE=$XSINK_URL\"\ngh auth switch --user pawan-dt >/dev/null 2>&1","description":"File cross-sink auto-create tracking issue"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2068,"cache_read_input_tokens":521917,"output_tokens":2745,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":706},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2068,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2745,"cache_read_input_tokens":521917,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2068,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2068},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeLvHBoy4GQ9cSSf3AkG7","type":"assistant","uuid":"b1cc9dec-59cc-4cfc-b509-8441fd62f3ae","timestamp":"2026-08-24T04:11:33.685Z","effort":"high","session_id":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream","sessionId":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","version":"2.1.228","gitBranch":"feat/bigquery-auto-create-table","slug":"linear-noodling-leaf"}
