{"parentUuid":"578dfef2-7baf-4bf3-96af-7fce015f4537","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CeLvXWnsZgBf1d7rWcaiH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013g2zjHjdksN5d9o2573Mc5","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream/docs/book/src/reference/config.md","offset":227,"limit":44},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":665,"cache_read_input_tokens":537924,"output_tokens":135,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":665,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":135,"cache_read_input_tokens":537924,"cache_creation_input_tokens":665,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":665},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeLvXUnZpv6GR7KygzrAX","type":"assistant","uuid":"0143256e-77fd-419b-8acf-c0bce54d91cd","timestamp":"2026-08-24T04:14:12.850Z","effort":"high","session_id":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream","sessionId":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","version":"2.1.228","gitBranch":"feat/bigquery-auto-create-table","slug":"linear-noodling-leaf"}
{"parentUuid":"0143256e-77fd-419b-8acf-c0bce54d91cd","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"a6953ba7-830f-4ac5-9194-491b45e02392","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013g2zjHjdksN5d9o2573Mc5","type":"tool_result","content":"227\t## `params`\n228\t\n229\tDeclares the config's **trigger-time** override surface: the values that change\n230\tper run, each typed. Referenced anywhere in the config as `${param.NAME}` and\n231\tbound *before* the config is parsed, so a param can never alter the document's\n232\tstructure and never reaches a connector unresolved.\n233\t\n234\t```yaml\n235\tparams:\n236\t  tenant_id: { type: string, required: true, description: \"Tenant to sync\" }\n237\t  since:     { default: \"1970-01-01\" }\n238\t  page_size: { type: int, default: 500 }\n239\t  api_token: { required: true, secret: true }\n240\t```\n241\t\n242\t| Field | Default | Meaning |\n243\t|---|---|---|\n244\t| `type` | `string` | `string` · `int` · `float` · `bool` |\n245\t| `required` | `false` | The caller must supply a value. Mutually exclusive with `default`. |\n246\t| `default` | — | Value when none is supplied. An ordinary config scalar, so `default: \"${env:SINCE}\"` resolves. |\n247\t| `secret` | `false` | Registered for redaction the instant it is bound — never reaches a log, error, API response, audit record, or the template registry. |\n248\t| `description` | — | Surfaced by `faucet template list`/`show`, `GET /v1/templates`, and the MCP `get_template` tool. |\n249\t\n250\t**Supplying values.** `faucet run --param name=value` (repeatable),\n251\t`faucet template run <id> --param …`, or `POST /v1/templates/{id}/runs` with a\n252\t`params` object. `--param-env NAME[=VALUE]` overrides an environment variable for\n253\tthat run's `${env:VAR}` resolution only, without mutating the process\n254\tenvironment.\n255\t\n256\t**Typing.** When `${param.NAME}` is a scalar's entire text the declared type\n257\tsurvives (an `int` param lands as a JSON number); embedded in a longer string it\n258\tis stringified, like every other namespace. Values are accepted as JSON (`500`)\n259\tor as strings (`\"500\"`) and coerced to the declared type, so CLI and HTTP behave\n260\tidentically. A type mismatch, a missing `required` param, an undeclared\n261\t`--param`, or an undeclared `${param.x}` reference is an error naming the param.\n262\t\n263\t**Validation.** `faucet validate` with no `--param` binds required params to\n264\ttype-shaped placeholders, so a parameterized config validates in CI without\n265\tinventing values; passing any `--param` switches to strict binding. `faucet\n266\tschema params` prints the JSON Schema for one entry.\n267\t\n268\tPersisting a parameterized config for register-once / trigger-by-id use is the\n269\t[pipeline template registry](../cookbook/templates.md).\n270\t"}]},"uuid":"9a5fa447-288c-4992-8abb-87b8837a5eff","timestamp":"2026-08-24T04:14:13.275Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream/docs/book/src/reference/config.md","content":"## `params`\n\nDeclares the config's **trigger-time** override surface: the values that change\nper run, each typed. Referenced anywhere in the config as `${param.NAME}` and\nbound *before* the config is parsed, so a param can never alter the document's\nstructure and never reaches a connector unresolved.\n\n```yaml\nparams:\n  tenant_id: { type: string, required: true, description: \"Tenant to sync\" }\n  since:     { default: \"1970-01-01\" }\n  page_size: { type: int, default: 500 }\n  api_token: { required: true, secret: true }\n```\n\n| Field | Default | Meaning |\n|---|---|---|\n| `type` | `string` | `string` · `int` · `float` · `bool` |\n| `required` | `false` | The caller must supply a value. Mutually exclusive with `default`. |\n| `default` | — | Value when none is supplied. An ordinary config scalar, so `default: \"${env:SINCE}\"` resolves. |\n| `secret` | `false` | Registered for redaction the instant it is bound — never reaches a log, error, API response, audit record, or the template registry. |\n| `description` | — | Surfaced by `faucet template list`/`show`, `GET /v1/templates`, and the MCP `get_template` tool. |\n\n**Supplying values.** `faucet run --param name=value` (repeatable),\n`faucet template run <id> --param …`, or `POST /v1/templates/{id}/runs` with a\n`params` object. `--param-env NAME[=VALUE]` overrides an environment variable for\nthat run's `${env:VAR}` resolution only, without mutating the process\nenvironment.\n\n**Typing.** When `${param.NAME}` is a scalar's entire text the declared type\nsurvives (an `int` param lands as a JSON number); embedded in a longer string it\nis stringified, like every other namespace. Values are accepted as JSON (`500`)\nor as strings (`\"500\"`) and coerced to the declared type, so CLI and HTTP behave\nidentically. A type mismatch, a missing `required` param, an undeclared\n`--param`, or an undeclared `${param.x}` reference is an error naming the param.\n\n**Validation.** `faucet validate` with no `--param` binds required params to\ntype-shaped placeholders, so a parameterized config validates in CI without\ninventing values; passing any `--param` switches to strict binding. `faucet\nschema params` prints the JSON Schema for one entry.\n\nPersisting a parameterized config for register-once / trigger-by-id use is the\n[pipeline template registry](../cookbook/templates.md).\n","numLines":44,"startLine":227,"totalLines":1185}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"0143256e-77fd-419b-8acf-c0bce54d91cd","session_id":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream","sessionId":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","version":"2.1.228","gitBranch":"feat/bigquery-auto-create-table","slug":"linear-noodling-leaf"}
