{"parentUuid":"11c7e562-3b4c-4bc2-b7c4-4f03ecdfe6a2","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"a6953ba7-830f-4ac5-9194-491b45e02392","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0176K19ZnMdxApesp4uZf3eS","type":"tool_result","content":"157\t### `${now.*}` — run-clock interpolation\n158\t\n159\t`${now.*}` tokens inject the current wall time into **source and sink config\n160\tvalues**. Each invocation evaluates them once at run time:\n161\t\n162\t| Token | Example output | Notes |\n163\t|-------|---------------|-------|\n164\t| `${now.date}` | `2026-03-08` | `YYYY-MM-DD` |\n165\t| `${now.datetime}` | `2026-03-08T14:05:09+00:00` | RFC 3339; alias: `${now.iso}` |\n166\t| `${now.iso}` | `2026-03-08T14:05:09+00:00` | Alias for `${now.datetime}` |\n167\t| `${now.year}` | `2026` | Zero-padded 4-digit year |\n168\t| `${now.month}` | `03` | Zero-padded month (01–12) |\n169\t| `${now.day}` | `08` | Zero-padded day (01–31) |\n170\t| `${now.hour}` | `14` | Zero-padded hour (00–23) |\n171\t| `${now.minute}` | `05` | Zero-padded minute (00–59) |\n172\t| `${now.second}` | `09` | Zero-padded second (00–59) |\n173\t| `${now.unix}` | `1741442709` | Unix epoch seconds |\n174\t| `${now.strftime.<fmt>}` | `2026/03/08/14` | Arbitrary [chrono strftime](https://docs.rs/chrono/latest/chrono/format/strftime/index.html) — e.g. `${now.strftime.%Y/%m/%d/%H}` |\n175\t\n176\tAn unknown token (e.g. `${now.foo}`) is a config error at run time. An invalid\n177\tstrftime format produces a clean config error rather than a panic.\n178\t\n179\t**Clock source:**\n180\t\n181\t- **`faucet run`** — the process start time in UTC. Override with\n182\t  `--clock <value>` for backfills: an RFC 3339 timestamp\n183\t  (`2026-03-01T00:00:00Z`) or a bare date (`2026-03-01`, treated as midnight\n184\t  UTC). See the [`run` command reference](cli.md#run).\n185\t- **`faucet schedule`** — the tick's **scheduled time**, rendered in the\n186\t  schedule's `timezone`. `${now.date}` therefore reflects the date in the"}]},"uuid":"f3ae2c02-c0e4-43fd-bb18-25e3e05a9cf0","timestamp":"2026-08-24T04:23:38.829Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream/docs/book/src/reference/config.md","content":"### `${now.*}` — run-clock interpolation\n\n`${now.*}` tokens inject the current wall time into **source and sink config\nvalues**. Each invocation evaluates them once at run time:\n\n| Token | Example output | Notes |\n|-------|---------------|-------|\n| `${now.date}` | `2026-03-08` | `YYYY-MM-DD` |\n| `${now.datetime}` | `2026-03-08T14:05:09+00:00` | RFC 3339; alias: `${now.iso}` |\n| `${now.iso}` | `2026-03-08T14:05:09+00:00` | Alias for `${now.datetime}` |\n| `${now.year}` | `2026` | Zero-padded 4-digit year |\n| `${now.month}` | `03` | Zero-padded month (01–12) |\n| `${now.day}` | `08` | Zero-padded day (01–31) |\n| `${now.hour}` | `14` | Zero-padded hour (00–23) |\n| `${now.minute}` | `05` | Zero-padded minute (00–59) |\n| `${now.second}` | `09` | Zero-padded second (00–59) |\n| `${now.unix}` | `1741442709` | Unix epoch seconds |\n| `${now.strftime.<fmt>}` | `2026/03/08/14` | Arbitrary [chrono strftime](https://docs.rs/chrono/latest/chrono/format/strftime/index.html) — e.g. `${now.strftime.%Y/%m/%d/%H}` |\n\nAn unknown token (e.g. `${now.foo}`) is a config error at run time. An invalid\nstrftime format produces a clean config error rather than a panic.\n\n**Clock source:**\n\n- **`faucet run`** — the process start time in UTC. Override with\n  `--clock <value>` for backfills: an RFC 3339 timestamp\n  (`2026-03-01T00:00:00Z`) or a bare date (`2026-03-01`, treated as midnight\n  UTC). See the [`run` command reference](cli.md#run).\n- **`faucet schedule`** — the tick's **scheduled time**, rendered in the\n  schedule's `timezone`. `${now.date}` therefore reflects the date in the","numLines":30,"startLine":157,"totalLines":1205}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"11c7e562-3b4c-4bc2-b7c4-4f03ecdfe6a2","session_id":"55398